{"dir":"in","msg":{"emittedAtMs":1790704411393,"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"itemId":"4fdf781c-c6d0-415a-82ba-dc0ad189d8f6","kind":"agentMessage","recordedAt":"2026-09-29T17:53:31.392919Z","revision":2,"status":"completed","text":"Sum with common denominator 60, the LCM of 1 through 6:\n\n* 1 = 60/60\n* 1/2 = 30/60\n* 1/3 = 20/60\n* 1/4 = 15/60\n* 1/5 = 12/60\n* 1/6 = 10/60\n\nSum:\n\n`(60+30+20+15+12+10)/60 = 147/60`\n\nReduce: `147 = 3 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 7`, `60 = 2\u00b2 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 5`, so `gcd(147,60) = 3`.\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 3:\n\n`147/60 = 49/20`\n\n`49 = 7\u00b2` shares no prime factor with `20 = 2\u00b2 \u00d7 5`, so `gcd = 1`. It is in lowest terms.","turnId":"01a0ee4c-c559-75de-a972-7a91dbe59a8e"},"sessionId":"01a0ee4c-c501-7d50-9020-effa9f9956e1","sourceRange":{"first":{"id":"8e63bac4-b43a-435e-82e1-a0b124c9e62e","sequence":50},"last":{"id":"8e63bac4-b43a-435e-82e1-a0b124c9e62e","sequence":50},"stream":{"id":"01a0ee4c-c501-7d50-9020-effa9f9956e1","kind":"session"}},"viewCursor":"v:01a0ee4c-c501-7d50-9020-effa9f9956e1:7"}}}
